  "branch": "fix/bug-0079-merge-commit-msg",
  "bugRowUpdated": true,
  "diagnosis": "Reproduced: in a repo mid-merge (MERGE_HEAD set, merged branch added a docs/HISTORY entry), commit-msg diffs the index against HEAD (first parent), so the merged branch's own entry counts as added and its Subject differs from the merge subject; the hook blocks core/history-entry. Root cause: runCommitMsg in cli/git-commit-msg.ts never checks for a merge in progress, though SPEC 4.9.3 Exempt lists merge commits (and L4 judges only non-merge commits). Fix: skip the staged history judgment and the missing-entry check when MERGE_HEAD exists; still append the trailer.",
